<title>UK: Seton Healthcare acquires brand.</title>
<headline>Seton Healthcare acquires brand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British healthcare and sports products firm Seton Healthcare Group Plc said on Monday that it had acquired the gel brand, 'Metrotop' from Pharmacia and Upjohn Ltd for 3.75 million stg.</p>
<p>Seton's chief executive Iain Cater said the acquisition fitted with the company's existing range of wound dressing and infection control products.</p>
<p>'Metrotop' is used for malodorous and fungating wounds. The brand had reported sales of 1.02 million stg and an operating profit of 0.76 million stg in the year ended December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44-171-542 7717</p>
</text>
